 "root_notes": [
  "Under the contract's sealed rule, D6 closes on the plain HTML report from scripts/report.py. The one approved render attempt was not spent. The blocker was host contention during nix substitution and remote-builder copy-back (load averages up to about 530), not the fix. The direct probe shows the bundled pandoc 3.10 accepts the option that blocked D6. Whether to reopen D6 for its unused attempt in a quieter host window is an operator decision. The lane does not presume it.",
  "Merging flake.nix changes only the report devShell. default and analysis drvPaths are measured identical, so CI (nix develop --no-write-lock-file --command just ...) is unaffected.",
  "The quarto tarball is now a valid local store path. The bundled-pandoc output (188 MB) exists valid only on the remote builder petting-zoo-mini, and its local copy is partial (not valid)."
 ],
